/target
# Cargo.lock is TRACKED, not ignored: this package ships a `carve` binary,
# CI runs an MSRV leg, and the release workflow builds installable
# artifacts - all three want one resolved dependency set rather than
# whatever the registry serves that day. A committed lock file is ignored
# by anything that depends on `carve-lang`, so it constrains nobody
# downstream.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# stray local build artifact
/check

# Scratch: one-off patch scripts, notes and plans, by convention `_`-prefixed.
# They are working files for a single change and are worthless once it lands -
# `_fence.py` sat in the tree for months after the fix it applied was merged,
# and an automated PR later tried to "fix" the repo by editing it.
/_*
